,17.0,1992,53,96,25],[34020,17.1,1992,55,94,23],[34316,16.5,1961,57,96,23],[34317,16.6,1992,58,92,24],[34318,16.8,1992,54,88,27],[34319,16.7,1992,54,86,26]],"links":[["McHenry County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/north-dakota/mchenry-county"],["ARC or PLC in McHenry County","/arc-plc/north-dakota/mchenry-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years back to 1951, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 18 grids October to November came in under 90% of normal in 42 of them, the most of any pair. In 2025 that same pair ran 161% of normal on the middle, while January to February sat at 40%. So far in 2026, April to May came in at 41% of normal on the middle. Grid 33420 had its driest year in 1988 at 49%.</p>"}
